course: dictionary
lesson: 1393
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word car has more than one meaning, so the words around it tell you which one you need. Ask yourself what the sentence is about: a machine on the road, a part of a train, or a lift? This is the same skill as using context clues.
explain: «Small details like a car's colour, a number plate or what someone wore help police a lot.» Here car means a machine with four wheels and an engine, because a number plate only fits a road vehicle. Try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: People also use casual words for car, such as «wheels», «ride» and «banger» (an old car). These are fine with friends, but in a school report you would write car. Formal writing uses words like «motor vehicle» and «automobile».
explain: Car also appears in phrases such as «by car», «car seat» and «car sick». Read the whole phrase, not just one word, to find its meaning.
fact: Car means a machine with four wheels and an engine that people drive on roads.
fact: A car can also be one part of a train, like a dining car.
fact: In a lift or a cable car, the car is the part that carries people.
fact: «Banger» and «clunker» are casual words for an old car.
fact: Formal words for car include «motor vehicle» and «automobile» (USA).
exercise: «Small details like a car's colour, a number plate or what someone wore help police a lot.» In this sentence, what is a car? | A part of a train | A cable car on a mountain | A lift that carries people | *A machine with four wheels and an engine that people drive on roads
exercise: «For the same distance, flying on a big airline is much safer than going by car.» What does going by car mean? | *Travelling in a road vehicle | Parking the car near the airport | Buying a new engine | Carrying a car on a plane
exercise: A friend says he drives his old car, a banger. What does banger mean? | A new electric car | A loud firework | *An old car | A part of a train
test: «A boy in California crossed a street while looking at his phone; he never saw the car turning towards him.» What is the car in this sentence? | A dining car on a train | A lift that carries people | *A machine on the road that people drive | A cable car on a mountain
test: The sign says «car park», so you know it is a place for parking. What does car park mean? | *A place where cars are left | A room inside a lift | A station for cable cars | A park for dining cars
exam: In «so cars and railings by the sea rust quickly», what does cars mean? | Lifts in a tall building | Cable cars on a hill | *Machines with four wheels and an engine that people drive | Parts of a train
